---
description: Prevent misuse of mitmproxy `.log` files by treating them as binary and requiring proper tooling.
alwaysApply: true
---

### Enforce correct handling of `.log` files

- All `*.log` files in this project are **mitmproxy binary log files**, not plain text.
- Do **not** attempt to read, analyze, or filter them using plain text utilities such as `cat`, `grep`, `strings`, `sed`, `awk`, or similar tools. These commands will not work and may produce misleading results.
- Only use the supported tooling in `./tools/` to manipulate or inspect `.log` files.
  - Typical workflows include converting logs to JSON for analysis, or grepping HTTP flows using provided scripts.
- Any direct inspection or processing of `.log` files must be done through these supported tools, never with generic text-processing commands.
